  "arrangerNotes": "The 'Levee Song' as printed in the 1919 Brown Book (No. 54, in A♭; transcription saved as scores/b8/scan/levee_song_1919.ly), checked note by note. This is the familiar first part; the later 'Someone's in the kitchen with Dinah' section is a separate song and is not included. Words in standard spelling. Simplification: the one A natural (on 'hear' in 'Don't you hear the whistle blowing') is played as 1 (A♭). The score's rests are kept. Range low 5 to 4: C and D minLayout 11. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
  "verified": true
}
